y]]\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:carrot|carrots]], chopped\n* 1–2 [[Cookbook:zucchini|zucchini]], chopped\n* Vegetable or chicken soup mix or [[Cookbook:stock|stock]]\n* Salt\n* Pepper\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# [[Cookbook:Soaking Beans|Soak the beans]] for several hours and set aside.\n# In a large pot (the same one you'll make the soup in), [[Cookbook:Sautéing|sauté]] onion for about 3 minutes.\n# Add carrots and zucchini; sauté 5 minutes more.\n# Add mushrooms, and sauté until they release all their liquid.\n# Add the water, barley, beans, spices, and stock (or soup mix).\n# Cook for a few hours.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n* Mushrooms release a lot of liquid when cooking. You can add this liquid to the soup, as directed above, or boil it off to make more strongly flavored vegetables.\n* Cubed [[Cookbook:Meat and Poultry|meat]] can be added to this soup.\n\n[[Category:Recipes using mushroom]]\n[[Category:Recipes for soup]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units]]\n[[Category:Recipes using barley]]\n[[Category:Recipes using carrot]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mushroom Barley Bean Soup","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":"10","ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"10 cups (2400 ml) water","sourceText":"10 cups (2400 ml) water","amountText":"10 cups (2400 ml) water","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"1 medium onion, chopped","sourceText":"1 medium onion, chopped","amountText":"1 medium onion, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"8 oz (230 g) mushrooms, thickly sliced","sourceText":"8 oz (230 g) mushrooms, thickly sliced","amountText":"8 oz (230 g) mushrooms, thickly sliced","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"1 cup (240 ml) white beans","sourceText":"1 cup (240 ml) white beans","amountText":"1 cup (240 ml) white beans","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 cup (240 ml) barley","s